    "body": "## Summary\n- distinguish Stripe Connect transport failures from provider responses returned after Transfer/Payout activity that violate doFast's payout contract\n- quarantine known response anomalies instead of routing them through automatic provider retry\n- preserve only trusted Transfer/Payout references whose local payout identity matches; never attach a mismatched provider identity\n- keep reserved wallet funds untouched while the payout is in REVIEW_REQUIRED\n- allow a later signed, fully validated terminal Stripe webhook to resolve a reviewed payout without regressing webhook-wins races\n- retain the existing bounded same-idempotency-key retry path only for genuinely ambiguous/transport failures\n- add entity, provider, dispatcher, queue and settlement regression coverage\n\n## Financial invariant\nA known provider-side money-movement response must not be reclassified as a replayable transport failure. If provider identity is trustworthy, it may be retained for reconciliation; if identity mismatches, it must not be attached locally. In either case an anomalous response does not restore reserved funds and does not schedule another automatic Connect dispatch.\n\n## Schema\nNo Flyway migration. Existing provider_reference/provider_transfer_reference fields are reused.\n\n## Merge gate\nMerge only after exact-head API/Maven verify, frontend test/audit/lint/build, production Compose contract, full containers/runtime smoke, payment/payout financial smokes, CodeQL and container security are green. Before merge verify master is unchanged, branch is 0 behind and the PR head SHA is exactly the checked SHA.",
